membersFlagCapture -- the MEMBERs flag lands on another registry's original.

The MEMBERs flag command (Commands.rtn:516-517) runs at parse time, before aCTionDefinE, and sets
currentDefine.addingMembers = true -- where currentDefine (aCTionNewGroup) is the RESOLVED node. For a definition whose name
resolved to another registry's entry, the flag goes on the original's body. Today that is transient: aCTionDefinE clears it
at the end on NewGroup, and NewGroup's copy shares the original's body, so the clear reaches the original too. It becomes a
STUCK flag under any design that mints the definition its own node (the R2 try-and-buy, recon 19-20): the clear then hits
the fresh node and the original keeps addingMembers set, and every later definition in that registry reads as "adding
members". What this file shows live is the capture the flag rides on: the member mcKid lands in UnitTests' maximus.

